<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48125" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thĕŏdōrus</span></b> ,
		i, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Θεόδωρος.</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A Greek sophist of Byzantium</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Brut.
				12, 48</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Quint. 3, 1,
			11</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A Greek atheist of Cyrene</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D.
				1, 1, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Tusc. 1, 43, 102</span></i>; <i><span class="en">5, 40,
				117</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen. Tranq. 14,
			3</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A celebrated rhetorician of Gadara</i>, <i><span class="en">Quint. 3,
				1, 17</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 11,
				26</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Suet. Tib. 57</span></i>.—Hence,
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thĕ-ŏdōrēus</span></b> ,
				i, m., <i>a pupil and
				follower of Theodorus</i>, <i><span class="en">Quint. 2,
				11, 2</span></i>.—<i>Plur.</i>, <i><span class="en">Quint. 4,
				2, 32</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 1,
			18</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
